1
00:00:00,517 --> 00:00:03,413
I'll start by getting rid of
Mitsuru's things.

2
00:00:03,413 --> 00:00:05,049
As part of sorting out my emotions.

3
00:00:05,049 --> 00:00:07,153
You met each other
at a wedding ceremony, right?

4
00:00:07,153 --> 00:00:09,393
When we met, I was wearing this.

5
00:00:09,393 --> 00:00:11,425
Ah, the pizza's here.

6
00:00:12,489 --> 00:00:14,516
Coming!

7
00:00:18,349 --> 00:00:20,468
I'm home.

8
00:00:22,177 --> 00:00:24,598
Welcome back.

9
00:00:30,857 --> 00:00:33,349
Sorry.

10
00:00:33,349 --> 00:00:36,049
I threw away your slippers.

11
00:00:36,049 --> 00:00:39,389
It's okay. I'm wearing socks.

12
00:00:41,265 --> 00:00:42,953
Okay.

13
00:00:54,253 --> 00:00:56,133
A guest?

14
00:00:58,325 --> 00:01:00,429
A guest.

15
00:01:00,429 --> 00:01:02,977
Is it okay for me to be here?

16
00:01:13,241 --> 00:01:15,413
It's really you.

17
00:01:17,781 --> 00:01:19,713
Is there a fake me?

18
00:01:21,749 --> 00:01:25,021
That comeback is so you, Mitsuru.

19
00:01:28,653 --> 00:01:30,761
Mr. Sonoda is here.

20
00:01:32,037 --> 00:01:34,589
Mrs. Sonoda's husband?

21
00:01:35,381 --> 00:01:38,073
Yes, right.

22
00:01:38,073 --> 00:01:40,921
So the Sonoda you mentioned is Mrs. Sonoda?

23
00:01:40,921 --> 00:01:44,701
Is it okay for me to be here?

24
00:02:03,973 --> 00:02:05,869
Sorry.

25
00:02:07,221 --> 00:02:09,929
I felt like I should be the one
to hit you first after all.

26
00:02:13,493 --> 00:02:15,629
Next might be a fist.

27
00:02:16,861 --> 00:02:19,225
Make sure you clench your teeth.

28
00:02:20,681 --> 00:02:22,429
Okay.

29
00:02:25,049 --> 00:02:26,745
Mrs. Seo.

30
00:02:26,745 --> 00:02:29,037
About the bath towels,

31
00:02:29,037 --> 00:02:32,201
- the thick and the thin one, which one is...
- Oh, the bath towels...

32
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,793
This one is mine.

33
00:02:48,253 --> 00:02:49,897
Nice to meet you.

34
00:02:49,897 --> 00:02:52,233
My wife has been in your care.

35
00:03:04,597 --> 00:03:06,397
Likewise.

36
00:03:07,285 --> 00:03:09,757
My wife has been in your care.

37
00:03:19,937 --> 00:03:21,917
Oh, the pizza...

38
00:03:26,965 --> 00:03:29,045
Coming!

39
00:03:34,677 --> 00:03:38,289
[Episode 6]

40
00:03:38,289 --> 00:03:40,365
I'll make some tea.

41
00:03:40,365 --> 00:03:42,821
- Oh, I'm fine.
- Huh?

42
00:03:42,821 --> 00:03:45,877
I need to go pick up Sho soon.

43
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:47,609
Ah...

44
00:03:50,973 --> 00:03:54,641
I think you two should talk first.

45
00:03:54,641 --> 00:03:57,569
- Okay.
- Thank you for having me.

46
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:03,261
I'm sorry.

47
00:04:03,261 --> 00:04:05,481
I don't really understand
the situation either.

48
00:04:05,481 --> 00:04:06,589
I see.

49
00:04:06,589 --> 00:04:08,485
I'm sorry.

50
00:04:10,085 --> 00:04:12,725
I'll arrange a proper meeting another day,

51
00:04:12,725 --> 00:04:15,673
and get him to explain.

52
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:17,015
Okay.

53
00:04:17,015 --> 00:04:18,445
I'm sorry.

54
00:04:18,445 --> 00:04:20,233
Likewise.

55
00:04:20,233 --> 00:04:21,565
I'm sorry.

56
00:04:21,565 --> 00:04:23,649
I almost punched him just now.

57
00:04:23,649 --> 00:04:27,905
So I'll step away for a bit and cool down.

58
00:04:27,905 --> 00:04:29,801
I'm really sorry.

59
00:04:31,441 --> 00:04:34,307
Thank you for having me.

60
00:04:47,193 --> 00:04:48,947
Argh!

61
00:04:56,509 --> 00:04:58,221
Do you want some too, Sakiko?

62
00:04:59,485 --> 00:05:00,745
Yes.

63
00:05:00,745 --> 00:05:02,537
Okay.

64
00:05:18,593 --> 00:05:21,889
What are you thinking about right now?

65
00:05:23,201 --> 00:05:25,849
I want to go pay my respects
at Mrs. Sonoda's house,

66
00:05:25,849 --> 00:05:28,113
but I don't think today
is the best time for that.

67
00:05:28,113 --> 00:05:31,001
Besides, her husband is in that state.

68
00:05:32,437 --> 00:05:34,073
You're so calm.

69
00:05:34,073 --> 00:05:35,933
Am I?

70
00:05:36,981 --> 00:05:40,985
I'm thinking about what to ask you first.

71
00:05:42,461 --> 00:05:46,125
There's so much I want to ask,
so my head is a mess.

72
00:05:46,989 --> 00:05:48,713
You look calm.

73
00:05:48,713 --> 00:05:50,813
Well, I am an adult, after all.

74
00:05:51,917 --> 00:05:53,725
Mr. Sonoda too.

75
00:05:53,725 --> 00:05:57,753
He spoke calmly because he's an adult.

76
00:05:58,421 --> 00:06:00,289
He didn't hit anyone.

77
00:06:03,357 --> 00:06:04,909
An adult crying and screaming,

78
00:06:04,909 --> 00:06:08,273
or raising a hand, that's a big deal.

79
00:06:08,273 --> 00:06:10,433
You earlier, Sakiko,

80
00:06:11,217 --> 00:06:12,989
were at that point.

81
00:06:12,989 --> 00:06:14,693
Yeah.

82
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,521
I also thought it would be okay to hit you.

83
00:06:17,521 --> 00:06:19,349
I see.

84
00:06:23,325 --> 00:06:25,520
So...

85
00:06:26,237 --> 00:06:28,481
How do you feel now?

86
00:06:28,481 --> 00:06:29,721
Feel?

87
00:06:29,721 --> 00:06:32,649
What emotions are you feeling right now?

88
00:06:32,649 --> 00:06:35,645
I'm a little relieved.

89
00:06:36,269 --> 00:06:38,153
- That you didn't get hit?
- No.

90
00:06:38,153 --> 00:06:42,461
I'm relieved to see you
and Mrs. Sonoda's husband

91
00:06:42,461 --> 00:06:44,165
looking well.

92
00:06:58,913 --> 00:07:01,309
Do you know what I'm feeling right now?

93
00:07:02,865 --> 00:07:04,497
Mostly anger...

94
00:07:05,655 --> 00:07:07,581
I guess.

95
00:07:07,581 --> 00:07:09,409
Correct.

96
00:07:10,241 --> 00:07:12,489
I'm angry.

97
00:07:12,489 --> 00:07:14,341
Yeah.

98
00:07:15,381 --> 00:07:17,165
But...

99
00:07:18,417 --> 00:07:20,757
It's not just that. So I'm troubled.

100
00:07:23,145 --> 00:07:25,557
If it was just anger, it'd be fine.

101
00:07:25,557 --> 00:07:28,733
If I could have grabbed you
by the collar, choked you,

102
00:07:28,733 --> 00:07:31,881
if I could have stabbed you with a knife,
that would've been better.

103
00:07:33,357 --> 00:07:35,129
For me too,

104
00:07:35,801 --> 00:07:38,497
I'm relieved that you're looking well.

105
00:07:39,769 --> 00:07:42,661
And I'm happy that you came back.

106
00:07:42,661 --> 00:07:44,453
But...

107
00:07:45,521 --> 00:07:48,205
I'm scared to ask you what happened,

108
00:07:48,205 --> 00:07:50,645
and I'm worried about Mr. Sonoda too.

109
00:07:52,505 --> 00:07:55,069
I'd rather you just hadn't come back.

110
00:07:59,789 --> 00:08:02,853
But I'm also happy you came back.

111
00:08:02,853 --> 00:08:04,669
Happy to see you.

112
00:08:06,885 --> 00:08:11,485
And overall, I feel angry.

113
00:08:14,737 --> 00:08:17,065
Seeing you acting all nonchalant like that

114
00:08:18,961 --> 00:08:20,789
really makes me angry.

115
00:08:22,901 --> 00:08:24,625
I'm sorry.

116
00:08:24,625 --> 00:08:26,601
For what?

117
00:08:26,601 --> 00:08:28,357
Going missing?

118
00:08:29,109 --> 00:08:30,953
For Azusa?

119
00:08:34,373 --> 00:08:37,433
Don't go to Mr. Sonoda's house by yourself.

120
00:08:38,173 --> 00:08:41,045
Wait for when it's convenient for them,
and I'll go with you.

121
00:08:42,109 --> 00:08:43,973
Okay.

122
00:08:49,837 --> 00:08:52,005
Daddy!

123
00:08:52,005 --> 00:08:55,869
You're here! Welcome back!

124
00:08:56,985 --> 00:08:58,589
Daddy, you stink.

125
00:08:58,589 --> 00:09:00,465
Huh?

126
00:09:02,253 --> 00:09:05,109
I can't seem to get by without smoking.

127
00:09:06,425 --> 00:09:08,537
Did something bad happen?

128
00:09:09,237 --> 00:09:11,241
Yes.

129
00:09:11,241 --> 00:09:13,533
Are you okay?

130
00:09:13,533 --> 00:09:15,529
No.

131
00:09:18,757 --> 00:09:20,997
You can smoke if you want.

132
00:09:20,997 --> 00:09:22,533
It's okay.

133
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:24,961
You always want to smoke
when you drink coffee.

134
00:09:24,961 --> 00:09:27,797
It's fine. I won't get mad at you
at a time like this.

135
00:09:27,797 --> 00:09:30,309
I'm already pretty mad anyway.

136
00:09:30,309 --> 00:09:32,245
I won't get mad about that.

137
00:09:32,245 --> 00:09:34,161
No.

138
00:09:34,161 --> 00:09:37,393
I quit. I haven't smoked for a year.

139
00:09:37,393 --> 00:09:39,141
Really?

140
00:09:46,405 --> 00:09:48,789
What business did you have in Nagano?

141
00:09:49,633 --> 00:09:51,697
I went to see my parents.

142
00:09:53,521 --> 00:09:55,773
Then that address...

143
00:09:55,773 --> 00:09:57,401
That's my parents' house.

144
00:09:57,401 --> 00:09:59,585
I've been living there
with them this past year.

145
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:06,077
Are you okay?

146
00:10:08,805 --> 00:10:12,877
The person you met
at that house was my mother.

147
00:10:14,493 --> 00:10:15,721
I'm sorry.

148
00:10:15,721 --> 00:10:17,085
I told her that if someone
named Sakiko Seo came,

149
00:10:17,085 --> 00:10:20,661
she should pretend to not know anything,
no matter what you said.

150
00:10:22,669 --> 00:10:25,833
My father was there too.
He passed away recently, though.

151
00:10:27,505 --> 00:10:30,149
They're both indifferent people,

152
00:10:30,149 --> 00:10:32,101
but when my father died,

153
00:10:32,101 --> 00:10:34,229
my mother was really devastated,

154
00:10:34,229 --> 00:10:36,585
and that's when I remembered you.

155
00:10:38,089 --> 00:10:39,793
I disappeared so suddenly,

156
00:10:39,793 --> 00:10:42,449
I got worried about you
and how you were doing.

157
00:10:42,449 --> 00:10:45,077
Naoto came to help with the funeral,

158
00:10:45,077 --> 00:10:46,801
so I asked him then to arrange for me

159
00:10:46,801 --> 00:10:49,301
- to be able to talk to you on the phone.
- Wait.

160
00:10:51,937 --> 00:10:53,865
That's a lot of info.

161
00:10:58,433 --> 00:11:00,517
Or rather, the rest,

162
00:11:00,517 --> 00:11:02,977
I'll hear the rest together with Mr. Sonoda.

163
00:11:02,977 --> 00:11:05,757
Otherwise, you'd have to explain twice.

164
00:11:06,985 --> 00:11:09,717
- Okay.
- What are your plans for today?

165
00:11:10,373 --> 00:11:12,253
Are you staying over?

166
00:11:12,253 --> 00:11:14,609
Well, it is your house,
so I'm assuming you'll stay.

167
00:11:16,121 --> 00:11:18,113
Your underwear and stuff are in there.

168
00:11:19,405 --> 00:11:21,141
Yeah.

169
00:11:22,389 --> 00:11:24,819
Sorry, I was about to throw them away.

170
00:11:24,819 --> 00:11:26,529
It's fine.

171
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:34,597
Can I smoke?

172
00:11:34,597 --> 00:11:36,389
Sure, I guess.

173
00:11:52,649 --> 00:11:54,921
I can't taste anything at all.

174
00:11:59,577 --> 00:12:01,225
I'm going shopping. Need anything?

175
00:12:01,225 --> 00:12:03,257
Though it's just the usual supermarket.

176
00:12:03,257 --> 00:12:04,949
I'm fine.

177
00:12:04,949 --> 00:12:08,105
There isn't any sweet cheese.
I don't eat it, so I didn't buy any.

178
00:12:08,105 --> 00:12:10,009
Okay, then I want some.

179
00:12:10,009 --> 00:12:11,761
I'm off.

180
00:12:12,693 --> 00:12:14,329
It's fine, you can eat that.

181
00:12:14,329 --> 00:12:15,837
Okay, thanks.

182
00:12:15,837 --> 00:12:16,997
Take care.

183
00:12:16,997 --> 00:12:18,745
Yeah.

184
00:12:22,861 --> 00:12:26,953
<i>No matter how much we explain our feelings,</i>

185
00:12:26,953 --> 00:12:29,701
<i>it still feels like something
is off from the truth.</i>

186
00:12:33,177 --> 00:12:35,605
<i>Mitsuru went to see his parents.</i>

187
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:40,369
<i>He's been living with them for the past year.</i>

188
00:12:40,369 --> 00:12:42,193
<i>He had quit smoking.</i>

189
00:12:45,637 --> 00:12:49,141
<i>I felt like everything ever since
our first encounter was being denied.</i>

190
00:12:49,141 --> 00:12:50,781
<i>And now, from the couple,</i>

191
00:12:50,781 --> 00:12:55,465
<i>a bouquet of gratitude for the parents!</i>

192
00:13:04,913 --> 00:13:07,529
It's nice how close they are
as families, huh?

193
00:13:07,529 --> 00:13:09,373
Yeah, it is.

194
00:13:11,809 --> 00:13:14,305
<i>And now, the bride, Ami,</i>

195
00:13:14,305 --> 00:13:18,889
<i>has written a letter
expressing her gratitude to her parents.</i>

196
00:13:18,889 --> 00:13:20,333
I'm stepping out, just to the bathroom.

197
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:23,361
- Huh? Now?
- Sorry, I can't hold it.

198
00:13:25,145 --> 00:13:28,593
<i>Dad, Mom...</i>

199
00:13:51,429 --> 00:13:55,441
They're reading the letter to Ami's parents
right now. It's a good part.

200
00:13:55,441 --> 00:13:57,269
Yes.

201
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:08,325
Even though it's a good part,
is it still okay to leave?

202
00:14:09,097 --> 00:14:11,644
I...

203
00:14:11,644 --> 00:14:13,057
I ran away.

204
00:14:13,057 --> 00:14:15,705
Ah, same here.

205
00:14:15,705 --> 00:14:19,173
- Same?
- Yes, I find those things unpleasant.

206
00:14:19,173 --> 00:14:22,217
Whether I'm there or not,
it doesn't make any difference.

207
00:14:22,217 --> 00:14:26,245
And I'd feel bad disturbing those
who are genuinely moved.

208
00:14:28,765 --> 00:14:30,505
Right.

209
00:14:32,509 --> 00:14:34,877
Are you from the groom's side?

210
00:14:34,877 --> 00:14:36,185
I'm from the company.

211
00:14:36,185 --> 00:14:39,345
I'm a high school classmate of Ami's.

212
00:14:42,525 --> 00:14:45,589
Will you go back
after you finish that cigarette?

213
00:14:45,589 --> 00:14:49,497
Yes. Though I don't really have to go back.

214
00:14:50,117 --> 00:14:52,365
I get it.

215
00:14:52,365 --> 00:14:56,009
I'm not exactly dying to go back either.

216
00:14:58,461 --> 00:15:00,841
I dread the after-party.

217
00:15:00,841 --> 00:15:04,017
Yeah, the after-party really is a drag.

218
00:15:05,177 --> 00:15:06,569
Will the parents attend that too?

219
00:15:06,569 --> 00:15:08,061
Seems like it.

220
00:15:08,061 --> 00:15:10,169
Like, it seems like
they're all quite close as families.

221
00:15:10,169 --> 00:15:13,237
Seriously? That stinks.

222
00:15:13,237 --> 00:15:16,729
Yeah, I totally get it.

223
00:15:17,377 --> 00:15:19,885
I wonder if she's done reading yet?

224
00:15:19,885 --> 00:15:21,621
Yeah.

225
00:15:22,417 --> 00:15:24,789
Wanna go somewhere? Just the two of us?

226
00:15:30,081 --> 00:15:32,533
Oh, don't go back.

227
00:15:33,609 --> 00:15:35,857
Like, maybe we could go get a drink?

228
00:15:40,193 --> 00:15:43,817
If we suddenly disappear,
everyone will worry.

229
00:15:45,157 --> 00:15:47,493
Right, sorry.

230
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:56,401
Well, then.

231
00:16:02,841 --> 00:16:04,645
Well...

232
00:16:05,621 --> 00:16:07,205
would here be okay?

233
00:16:07,205 --> 00:16:08,341
Huh?

234
00:16:08,341 --> 00:16:10,173
I'll be waiting here after the after-party.

235
00:16:10,173 --> 00:16:12,069
It's close by.

236
00:16:14,073 --> 00:16:16,485
Okay.

237
00:16:16,485 --> 00:16:19,705
I'll have one more cigarette
and then head back.

238
00:16:21,837 --> 00:16:22,857
<i>What a weird guy.</i>

239
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:24,437
Congratulations on your wedding.

240
00:16:24,437 --> 00:16:29,217
<i>But in a group, he seemed normal.</i>

241
00:16:29,217 --> 00:16:32,369
<i>He blended in naturally.</i>

242
00:16:32,369 --> 00:16:35,101
<i>I thought he was a weird guy
who could act normal.</i>

243
00:16:35,101 --> 00:16:36,985
- Shall we go? Let's go.
- Huh? Okay, let's go.

244
00:16:48,477 --> 00:16:50,741
Welcome.

245
00:16:50,741 --> 00:16:52,933
Oh, thanks for coming.

246
00:16:54,285 --> 00:16:57,565
Even if we're not having fun,
we end up pretending to be.

247
00:16:57,565 --> 00:17:00,501
It's no use sulking.

248
00:17:00,501 --> 00:17:02,101
Exactly.

249
00:17:02,101 --> 00:17:06,677
In the end, it's easier to just
act like an adult.

250
00:17:08,373 --> 00:17:10,353
But sneaking out like that...

251
00:17:11,185 --> 00:17:12,613
Yeah.

252
00:17:12,613 --> 00:17:16,189
I just couldn't handle it today.

253
00:17:16,189 --> 00:17:17,282
Another one, please.

254
00:17:17,282 --> 00:17:19,057
Certainly.

255
00:17:20,345 --> 00:17:23,225
<i>It's not that we clicked especially well.</i>

256
00:17:23,225 --> 00:17:27,453
<i>But strangely, we never
ran out of things to talk about.</i>

257
00:17:27,453 --> 00:17:31,137
<i>And the occasional
little silences were comfortable.</i>

258
00:17:31,137 --> 00:17:35,673
<i>I talked about 60% of the time,
he talked about 40%.</i>

259
00:17:35,673 --> 00:17:38,189
You're not very good with
those kinds of letters.

260
00:17:38,189 --> 00:17:39,697
Yeah.

261
00:17:39,697 --> 00:17:41,877
Me neither.

262
00:17:41,877 --> 00:17:45,609
I'm not really that close with my parents.

263
00:17:45,609 --> 00:17:46,905
How should I put it?

264
00:17:46,905 --> 00:17:49,285
It's not exactly out of jealousy,

265
00:17:49,285 --> 00:17:51,165
but... well, maybe it is out of jealousy?

266
00:17:52,833 --> 00:17:55,777
Whenever I see a close family,

267
00:17:55,777 --> 00:17:58,817
I feel like I'm missing something.

268
00:18:00,261 --> 00:18:01,769
That's it.

269
00:18:01,769 --> 00:18:04,576
I feel like I'm defective.

270
00:18:04,576 --> 00:18:06,505
It's painful to watch them.

271
00:18:06,505 --> 00:18:09,942
Close families, people who are
good to their parents,

272
00:18:09,942 --> 00:18:13,325
parents who cherish their kids, all of that.

273
00:18:14,589 --> 00:18:16,497
Yes.

274
00:18:17,209 --> 00:18:19,385
That's exactly it.

275
00:18:19,385 --> 00:18:21,777
<i>It was a feeling I'd had for years,</i>

276
00:18:21,777 --> 00:18:25,037
<i>but never been able to put into words.</i>

277
00:18:25,037 --> 00:18:30,013
I'm estranged from my parents.
I haven't seen them in about 15 years.

278
00:18:30,013 --> 00:18:31,665
They're indifferent people,

279
00:18:31,665 --> 00:18:35,501
so if I don't reach out,
we become strangers in no time.

280
00:18:35,501 --> 00:18:37,633
Huh.

281
00:18:37,633 --> 00:18:41,573
In my case, my mom is overly controlling,

282
00:18:41,573 --> 00:18:45,112
and she pushes things on me thinking
they're good for me, even if I hate them.

283
00:18:45,112 --> 00:18:50,145
And if I reject them,
she either cries or gets hysterical.

284
00:18:50,145 --> 00:18:53,777
And just when I think she's calmed down,

285
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:57,153
she starts this big speech about how hard
it was to give birth to me and raise me.

286
00:18:57,153 --> 00:19:00,141
A long lecture.

287
00:19:00,141 --> 00:19:02,153
Huh.

288
00:19:02,153 --> 00:19:03,753
That must be painful too.

289
00:19:03,753 --> 00:19:06,397
Like you're the bad one for not accepting it.

290
00:19:06,397 --> 00:19:07,701
Yes.

291
00:19:07,701 --> 00:19:09,173
You're listening to me.

292
00:19:09,173 --> 00:19:11,005
- Yes.
- For me,

293
00:19:11,005 --> 00:19:15,061
in second grade, that was the first time
I thought my mom might be weird.

294
00:19:15,061 --> 00:19:19,321
She tried to pick and choose my friends.

295
00:19:19,321 --> 00:19:22,325
<i>I could share this feeling with him.</i>

296
00:19:22,961 --> 00:19:25,077
<i>I was happy.</i>

297
00:19:25,077 --> 00:19:27,181
I wish I had an older sibling.

298
00:19:27,181 --> 00:19:29,641
Someone to look up to, I guess.

299
00:19:29,641 --> 00:19:31,969
Right. Like, under these parents,

300
00:19:31,969 --> 00:19:35,493
how to live, and how things become.

301
00:19:35,493 --> 00:19:36,693
Like a sample?

302
00:19:36,693 --> 00:19:38,125
Exactly.

303
00:19:38,125 --> 00:19:40,153
That doesn't sound very nice, though.

304
00:19:42,673 --> 00:19:44,705
Are you taking the train home?

305
00:19:44,705 --> 00:19:47,793
- Yes.
- Then shall we head out soon?

306
00:19:50,757 --> 00:19:52,493
Okay.

307
00:19:54,721 --> 00:19:57,649
- Check, please.
- Yes, thank you.

308
00:19:58,717 --> 00:20:01,261
You can treat me next time.

309
00:20:01,261 --> 00:20:02,629
Next time?

310
00:20:02,629 --> 00:20:04,681
Yes.

311
00:20:07,109 --> 00:20:09,381
Okay.

312
00:20:09,381 --> 00:20:12,241
<i>Maybe what was missing
in my past relationships</i>

313
00:20:12,241 --> 00:20:14,797
<i>was this feeling.</i>

314
00:20:21,657 --> 00:20:23,501
<i>With this person,</i>

315
00:20:24,233 --> 00:20:27,069
<i>I might be able to have a real family.</i>

316
00:20:29,905 --> 00:20:34,001
<i>On our third date, he suddenly proposed.</i>

317
00:20:34,001 --> 00:20:36,897
It's Sakiko, right? Your first name?

318
00:20:36,897 --> 00:20:39,153
- Yes.
- Between Little Saki and Sacchan,

319
00:20:39,153 --> 00:20:41,125
which do you prefer?

320
00:20:42,565 --> 00:20:44,797
When I was little,
people called me Little Saki.

321
00:20:44,797 --> 00:20:46,601
Friends?

322
00:20:46,601 --> 00:20:50,077
Most friends called me Saki,

323
00:20:50,077 --> 00:20:53,665
and relatives and neighbors
called me Little Saki.

324
00:20:54,961 --> 00:20:58,929
Then I'll call you Sacchan.

325
00:20:58,929 --> 00:21:00,577
Oh, okay.

326
00:21:00,577 --> 00:21:02,185
Then I guess that's settled.

327
00:21:02,185 --> 00:21:06,757
<i>Even before we dropped the formal speech,
he called me Sacchan.</i>

328
00:21:11,925 --> 00:21:14,685
[When can we meet next?]
<i>Just when I thought it might be going well,</i>

329
00:21:14,685 --> 00:21:16,817
<i>he stopped contacting me.</i>

330
00:21:19,293 --> 00:21:21,081
<i>One month passed,</i>

331
00:21:21,081 --> 00:21:23,229
<i>two months passed,</i>

332
00:21:23,962 --> 00:21:26,073
<i>and three months passed.</i>

333
00:21:27,741 --> 00:21:31,057
<i>Maybe he didn't like
that I still called him Mr. Seo?</i>

334
00:21:31,057 --> 00:21:33,893
<i>My nails may have been
a bit too flashy last time.</i>

335
00:21:34,569 --> 00:21:37,797
<i>Maybe ordering dessert
before being asked was a mistake.</i>

336
00:21:39,529 --> 00:21:42,101
<i>I regretted stupid little things.</i>

337
00:21:43,525 --> 00:21:46,373
<i>I suppose this could be
a side effect of love.</i>

338
00:21:48,741 --> 00:21:49,749
[Mitsuru Seo: Sorry for the delay.]

339
00:21:49,749 --> 00:21:51,452
[I just got back from an overseas
business trip. I'd love to see you again.]

340
00:21:53,537 --> 00:21:55,465
Sorry.

341
00:21:57,885 --> 00:21:59,145
[Mitsuru Seo: Sorry for the delay.]

342
00:21:59,145 --> 00:22:02,053
[I just got back from an overseas
business trip. I'd love to see you again.]

343
00:22:04,765 --> 00:22:08,105
<i>One notification on my phone,
and I was in a good mood.</i>

344
00:22:08,105 --> 00:22:10,061
<i>It was already love.</i>

345
00:22:11,529 --> 00:22:15,609
<i>We started dating
when 'Mr. Seo' became 'Mr. Mitsuru',</i>

346
00:22:15,609 --> 00:22:19,749
<i>and right after we got married,
'Mr. Mitsuru' became just 'Mitsuru'.</i>

347
00:22:21,253 --> 00:22:23,449
<i>We didn't have a wedding ceremony.</i>

348
00:22:24,945 --> 00:22:28,537
<i>We wanted to start our family
with just the two of us.</i>

349
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:31,169
You don't have to force yourself
to wear it normally.

350
00:22:31,169 --> 00:22:33,305
No, I'll wear it.

351
00:22:33,305 --> 00:22:35,601
It's a way to silently show
that we're married.

352
00:22:35,601 --> 00:22:37,109
Isn't that pretty convenient?

353
00:22:37,109 --> 00:22:39,137
I know, I thought the same thing.

354
00:22:39,137 --> 00:22:40,689
Right?

355
00:22:40,689 --> 00:22:42,649
Good.

356
00:22:42,649 --> 00:22:45,417
I didn't want to force you to wear it.

357
00:22:48,013 --> 00:22:50,977
<i>I had a feeling that
we could become a family.</i>

358
00:22:50,977 --> 00:22:52,985
- Sacchan.
- Hmm?

359
00:22:52,985 --> 00:22:54,073
Is it here?

360
00:22:54,073 --> 00:22:58,545
<i>The little frictions of living together
were all within expectations,</i>

361
00:22:58,545 --> 00:23:01,277
<i>and we could easily resolve them by talking.</i>

362
00:23:03,641 --> 00:23:05,437
- Hey.
- Hmm?

363
00:23:05,437 --> 00:23:07,381
Is it the pumpkin?

364
00:23:08,873 --> 00:23:10,697
Sorry, but I don't like pumpkin.

365
00:23:11,825 --> 00:23:13,429
Sorry.

366
00:23:13,429 --> 00:23:16,053
<i>We had only one rule.</i>

367
00:23:16,053 --> 00:23:17,733
<i>No lying.</i>

368
00:23:17,733 --> 00:23:20,721
<i>But neither of us had to talk about anything
that we didn't want to talk about.</i>

369
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,349
<i>It was simple.</i>

370
00:23:24,349 --> 00:23:27,129
I'll have my baby and come back healthy.

371
00:23:27,129 --> 00:23:31,333
<i>What was hard was
no longer being just the two of us.</i>

372
00:23:32,337 --> 00:23:33,605
Welcome back.

373
00:23:33,605 --> 00:23:35,581
<i>Three is better than two,</i>

374
00:23:35,581 --> 00:23:37,877
<i>and four is better than three.</i>

375
00:23:37,877 --> 00:23:40,044
<i>I imagined too much that it was
what a family should be like.</i>

376
00:23:40,044 --> 00:23:42,489
[Pregnancy test]

377
00:23:46,109 --> 00:23:49,877
<i>Even though we were happy
as just two, I got greedy.</i>

378
00:23:57,441 --> 00:24:00,421
I'm also happy with just the two of us.

379
00:24:04,965 --> 00:24:07,365
Just three more days' worth.

380
00:24:07,365 --> 00:24:09,365
I'll finish these off.

381
00:24:13,825 --> 00:24:15,773
Thank you.

382
00:24:18,753 --> 00:24:19,965
Whoa!

383
00:24:19,965 --> 00:24:23,205
<i>We bought a house just for the two of us.</i>

384
00:24:23,205 --> 00:24:25,089
This feels good.

385
00:24:27,049 --> 00:24:28,957
Nice, isn't it?

386
00:24:29,733 --> 00:24:32,397
<i>We were happy.</i>

387
00:24:32,397 --> 00:24:36,353
<i>I thought we could live together forever
in this house, just the two of us.</i>

388
00:24:36,353 --> 00:24:39,025
<i>I really thought we could.</i>

389
00:24:41,493 --> 00:24:43,449
<i>What did we do wrong?</i>

390
00:24:44,489 --> 00:24:46,973
<i>What was wrong with me?</i>

391
00:24:50,409 --> 00:24:52,345
<i>Or...</i>

392
00:24:54,477 --> 00:24:56,893
<i>did you find another right answer?</i>

393
00:24:59,469 --> 00:25:01,705
Welcome back.

394
00:25:01,705 --> 00:25:02,717
I'm home.

395
00:25:02,717 --> 00:25:05,069
That must have been heavy, right? Thanks.

396
00:25:12,769 --> 00:25:14,541
Did you clean the floor?

397
00:25:14,541 --> 00:25:16,905
Yeah, lightly.

398
00:25:16,905 --> 00:25:18,965
Thanks.

399
00:25:18,965 --> 00:25:21,541
That thing's not doing very well, is it?

400
00:25:22,349 --> 00:25:25,501
Yeah, it's been like that for a while.

401
00:25:28,261 --> 00:25:32,433
It stops as soon as you move it a bit.
Is it on its last legs?

402
00:25:32,433 --> 00:25:34,101
Probably.

403
00:25:34,101 --> 00:25:37,009
The warranty period for repairs has passed.

404
00:25:37,009 --> 00:25:38,226
Five years?

405
00:25:38,226 --> 00:25:39,629
Yeah.

406
00:25:39,629 --> 00:25:43,093
Even though we paid an extra
2,000 yen or something, that's expired too.

407
00:25:43,093 --> 00:25:45,073
I see.

408
00:25:45,073 --> 00:25:48,881
I tried cleaning the filter,
but it was totally clean.

409
00:25:48,881 --> 00:25:50,101
You mean for the washing machine?

410
00:25:50,101 --> 00:25:53,109
Huh? No, for the vacuum cleaner.

411
00:25:53,773 --> 00:25:55,666
Oh.

412
00:25:56,605 --> 00:25:58,617
Is there anything else you need done?

413
00:25:58,617 --> 00:26:00,969
Places you can't reach?

414
00:26:00,969 --> 00:26:02,757
Oh, what about the winter clothes?

415
00:26:02,757 --> 00:26:04,637
Did you put them on the top shelf?

416
00:26:07,521 --> 00:26:09,413
Sacchan?

417
00:26:17,507 --> 00:26:19,324
Sacchan?

418
00:26:31,793 --> 00:26:34,285
This is what I wanted.

419
00:26:39,293 --> 00:26:41,217
Just the two of us here,

420
00:26:42,533 --> 00:26:46,241
talking about boring stuff like this forever.

421
00:26:48,393 --> 00:26:50,809
About food, appliances.

422
00:26:52,417 --> 00:26:55,409
I thought this would go on forever.

423
00:27:08,321 --> 00:27:11,149
Since it's not related to Mr. Sonoda,

424
00:27:11,961 --> 00:27:14,309
there's something I want to ask you
while it's just the two of us.

425
00:27:15,513 --> 00:27:17,410
Okay.

426
00:27:19,905 --> 00:27:22,321
What did you dislike about me?

427
00:27:24,401 --> 00:27:26,137
Is it because of kids?

428
00:27:34,465 --> 00:27:36,241
Okay, if not then what?

429
00:27:38,413 --> 00:27:40,545
- Sacchan...
- Saying that I didn't do anything wrong,

430
00:27:40,545 --> 00:27:43,661
that's the worst.

431
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:47,613
Because it means that
there's nothing I can do.

432
00:27:49,553 --> 00:27:52,837
It means that you found someone else,
someone who isn't me.

433
00:27:54,097 --> 00:27:56,421
That's the worst.

434
00:28:03,409 --> 00:28:07,293
I see, that's it.

435
00:28:09,209 --> 00:28:11,141
That's it, isn't it?

436
00:28:16,045 --> 00:28:17,797
Where's your ring?

437
00:28:19,849 --> 00:28:21,837
I have it.

438
00:28:21,837 --> 00:28:23,621
I just don't wear it.

439
00:28:56,301 --> 00:28:58,065
Mrs. Seo.

440
00:29:00,441 --> 00:29:02,621
Oh, Mr. Sonoda.

441
00:29:02,621 --> 00:29:04,805
You startled me.

442
00:29:07,513 --> 00:29:09,657
Doing laundry?

443
00:29:09,657 --> 00:29:10,905
No, you aren't, are you?

444
00:29:10,905 --> 00:29:12,401
Yeah.

445
00:29:12,401 --> 00:29:13,805
Just taking a walk, I guess.

446
00:29:13,805 --> 00:29:16,977
Ah, same here.

447
00:29:16,977 --> 00:29:18,965
Where's Mitsuru?

448
00:29:18,965 --> 00:29:20,665
At home.

449
00:29:20,665 --> 00:29:23,057
I get restless when we're alone together.

450
00:29:23,057 --> 00:29:25,657
Yeah, I bet.

451
00:29:25,657 --> 00:29:27,481
It was so sudden.

452
00:29:28,213 --> 00:29:31,481
I know we have to talk,

453
00:29:31,481 --> 00:29:35,849
but the things I want to ask
are scary and hard to ask.

454
00:29:37,621 --> 00:29:42,561
I ask a little, get really shaken, explode,

455
00:29:42,561 --> 00:29:44,457
and that led to this walk.

456
00:29:45,341 --> 00:29:48,549
I'm scared to hear the details too.

457
00:29:48,549 --> 00:29:49,917
Yes.

458
00:29:49,917 --> 00:29:51,769
Oh, how's Sho?

459
00:29:51,769 --> 00:29:53,921
My sister's looking after him.

460
00:29:53,921 --> 00:29:56,849
He had swimming today,
so he went to sleep right away.

461
00:29:56,849 --> 00:29:59,645
He said he'll show me
the butterfly stroke next time.

462
00:29:59,645 --> 00:30:01,553
What's that about? When's that gonna be?

463
00:30:01,553 --> 00:30:03,453
Well, he can't do it yet.

464
00:30:03,453 --> 00:30:05,393
He was talking about it
like it's his specialty.

465
00:30:05,393 --> 00:30:06,789
Huh?

466
00:30:06,789 --> 00:30:08,501
Huh?

467
00:30:18,725 --> 00:30:22,405
I feel calm when I'm with you, Mr. Sonoda.

468
00:30:23,725 --> 00:30:25,689
Oh, I didn't mean anything deep by that.

469
00:30:25,689 --> 00:30:27,005
No, I know.

470
00:30:27,005 --> 00:30:30,249
It's just as you said.
No fluttering or restlessness.

471
00:30:30,249 --> 00:30:32,361
That's right.

472
00:30:32,361 --> 00:30:33,753
I'm sorry.

473
00:30:33,753 --> 00:30:36,597
Well, being laughed at is a little annoying.

474
00:30:37,977 --> 00:30:40,753
I'm grateful that

475
00:30:40,753 --> 00:30:42,769
nothing can shake my heart.

476
00:30:42,769 --> 00:30:45,593
I'm of that same mindset now.

477
00:30:45,593 --> 00:30:48,477
You alone don't shake my heart, Mrs. Seo.

478
00:30:48,477 --> 00:30:50,509
Me alone?

479
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:59,965
Honestly, whatever happens,
Azusa isn't coming back,

480
00:31:01,293 --> 00:31:04,697
so I thought that if this could continue,
that would be nice.

481
00:31:05,805 --> 00:31:10,061
Every Saturday,
talking nonsense with you here,

482
00:31:10,061 --> 00:31:12,969
and occasionally having dinner with Sho too.

483
00:31:14,065 --> 00:31:16,433
I guess I'm just wishing for
the impossible again.

484
00:31:17,977 --> 00:31:21,077
I was thinking about
tracking him down and punching him,

485
00:31:21,077 --> 00:31:22,917
but when he actually showed up...

486
00:31:24,277 --> 00:31:26,133
Mitsuru...

487
00:31:28,505 --> 00:31:32,201
He didn't say there was anything
about me that he disliked.

488
00:31:35,401 --> 00:31:37,477
Which means it's about Azusa.

489
00:31:40,401 --> 00:31:42,201
And if that's the case,

490
00:31:42,201 --> 00:31:45,661
we need to talk,
with you included, Mr. Sonoda.

491
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:49,565
When should we do it? The talk.

492
00:31:51,505 --> 00:31:53,677
Though it's not really a talk, is it?

493
00:31:54,733 --> 00:31:56,941
More like an interrogation.

494
00:31:59,101 --> 00:32:01,433
Mrs. Seo.

495
00:32:01,433 --> 00:32:02,741
Hmm?

496
00:32:02,741 --> 00:32:04,781
Did you cry?

497
00:32:09,637 --> 00:32:11,453
Yes.

498
00:32:13,061 --> 00:32:14,908
Earlier...

499
00:32:16,030 --> 00:32:17,657
And pretty hard.

500
00:32:20,609 --> 00:32:22,461
Did you get angry?

501
00:32:23,633 --> 00:32:25,161
Yes.

502
00:32:25,161 --> 00:32:28,209
Oh, I didn't mention this before,

503
00:32:28,209 --> 00:32:29,902
but I...

504
00:32:30,864 --> 00:32:33,521
I hit him first.

505
00:32:33,521 --> 00:32:34,929
Though it was just a slap.

506
00:32:34,929 --> 00:32:36,759
Oh, then...

507
00:32:37,651 --> 00:32:39,049
I'm glad.

508
00:32:39,049 --> 00:32:40,865
Sorry.

509
00:32:48,513 --> 00:32:50,829
How about tomorrow night?

510
00:32:50,829 --> 00:32:52,657
Better to do it sooner.

511
00:32:52,657 --> 00:32:55,349
I'll figure out something for Sho.

512
00:32:57,393 --> 00:32:59,109
- Okay.
- Yeah.

513
00:33:23,945 --> 00:33:25,801
- Every year?
- Yes.

514
00:33:53,545 --> 00:33:55,925
Welcome back.

515
00:33:55,925 --> 00:33:57,673
I'm home.

516
00:34:00,545 --> 00:34:02,257
Good night.

517
00:34:07,301 --> 00:34:09,013
Good night.

518
00:34:13,533 --> 00:34:15,441
Please take care of it.

519
00:34:17,189 --> 00:34:19,733
Well, Chizuru?

520
00:34:19,733 --> 00:34:22,657
Shall we meet at the usual place tonight?

521
00:34:22,657 --> 00:34:24,137
There's so much I want to talk about,

522
00:34:24,137 --> 00:34:27,693
I feel like I have to finish work
right now and go drinking,

523
00:34:27,693 --> 00:34:29,809
but I'll try to hold out
until the end of the day.

524
00:34:29,809 --> 00:34:32,573
Oh, sorry.

525
00:34:32,573 --> 00:34:34,793
Tonight's not going to work.

526
00:34:34,793 --> 00:34:36,389
Huh?

527
00:34:36,389 --> 00:34:40,377
Sorry, I just really need a rain check.

528
00:34:40,377 --> 00:34:43,981
What? Did Mitsuru come home or something?

529
00:34:43,981 --> 00:34:46,473
I won't accept any excuse less than that.

530
00:34:47,729 --> 00:34:49,545
That's it.

531
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:51,013
Huh?

532
00:34:51,013 --> 00:34:52,937
He came home.

533
00:34:52,937 --> 00:34:54,681
I'm glad you're okay.

534
00:34:54,681 --> 00:34:56,597
Well, I did get slapped.

535
00:34:57,489 --> 00:34:59,529
You could have been stabbed, you know.

536
00:34:59,529 --> 00:35:03,657
Thank goodness Sacchan is an adult
who can keep her cool.

537
00:35:05,857 --> 00:35:08,981
In this kind of situation,
that kind of phrasing

538
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:11,937
can really make people angry.

539
00:35:12,585 --> 00:35:15,489
Please choose your words more carefully.

540
00:35:15,489 --> 00:35:16,702
This past year,

541
00:35:16,702 --> 00:35:18,437
the number of people
I interacted with drastically decreased,

542
00:35:18,437 --> 00:35:21,017
so it seems my communication skills
have gotten worse.

543
00:35:21,661 --> 00:35:25,373
Even though I've survived
just thanks to my good external appearance.

544
00:35:29,761 --> 00:35:32,857
I'm glad that you've been here, Naoto.

545
00:35:32,857 --> 00:35:34,769
If you hadn't been here,
I might not have run away.

546
00:35:34,769 --> 00:35:37,209
Or if I had run away,
I might have come back sooner.

547
00:35:37,945 --> 00:35:39,329
So from Sakiko's perspective,

548
00:35:39,329 --> 00:35:42,229
that means it would have been better
if I hadn't been here.

549
00:35:42,229 --> 00:35:45,521
It would've turned out
like this eventually anyway.

550
00:35:45,521 --> 00:35:49,009
How long has it been? How long really?

551
00:35:49,009 --> 00:35:50,917
It was right around when I met Sacchan.

552
00:35:50,917 --> 00:35:53,165
About ten years ago.

553
00:35:53,165 --> 00:35:55,161
That's amazing, isn't it?

554
00:35:55,981 --> 00:35:58,401
No, Sakiko is the amazing one.

555
00:35:59,085 --> 00:36:02,185
Thanks to her, I was able to stay
in one place for this long.

556
00:36:02,857 --> 00:36:04,633
Look.

557
00:36:07,817 --> 00:36:09,561
You're good.

558
00:36:10,237 --> 00:36:12,241
I'll give it to the old man.

559
00:36:15,053 --> 00:36:17,561
I didn't bring any gifts.

560
00:36:18,189 --> 00:36:20,117
Is this okay?

561
00:36:20,813 --> 00:36:23,697
I'll buy something on the way back.

562
00:36:23,697 --> 00:36:26,641
Give this to the old man too.

563
00:36:26,641 --> 00:36:28,369
Okay.

564
00:36:31,145 --> 00:36:36,449
Sho, if you could talk to Mommy,
what would you say?

565
00:36:36,449 --> 00:36:37,937
Anything?

566
00:36:37,937 --> 00:36:39,761
Yeah, anything.

567
00:36:41,497 --> 00:36:44,057
Mommy!

568
00:36:44,057 --> 00:36:47,365
You're back!

569
00:36:53,025 --> 00:36:54,951
Right?

570
00:36:58,253 --> 00:37:00,569
See, there's the old man.

571
00:37:00,569 --> 00:37:03,969
- Hello.
- Oh, you're here.

572
00:37:03,969 --> 00:37:06,909
- This is for you.
- Oh, for me?

573
00:37:06,909 --> 00:37:10,897
Well, this is a bit clumsy,
just like your mom.

574
00:37:10,897 --> 00:37:14,488
But it has character. Thank you.

575
00:37:17,781 --> 00:37:20,257
All right, then,
please look after him for a bit.

576
00:37:20,257 --> 00:37:22,317
I wonder if it'll turn into a bloodbath.

577
00:37:25,221 --> 00:37:27,181
Tell me about it later.

578
00:37:28,249 --> 00:37:30,373
Let's do our best.

579
00:37:42,725 --> 00:37:47,133
Okay, Mitsuru, please answer everything
you're asked properly.

580
00:37:47,133 --> 00:37:48,877
Got it.

581
00:37:51,701 --> 00:37:56,445
Why was my wife with you that day?

582
00:37:56,445 --> 00:37:59,561
I heard you were going to see your parents.

583
00:37:59,561 --> 00:38:02,893
Why was my wife accompanying you
for something like that?

584
00:38:02,893 --> 00:38:04,913
I don't think it'd be relevant
to have her along.

585
00:38:07,033 --> 00:38:11,049
About a year before the accident,

586
00:38:11,049 --> 00:38:12,764
I met Mrs. Sonoda at the laundromat,

587
00:38:12,764 --> 00:38:15,609
and we often talked
on the third Friday of every month.

588
00:38:16,757 --> 00:38:17,949
And?

589
00:38:17,949 --> 00:38:20,121
When I met her the day before the accident,

590
00:38:20,121 --> 00:38:22,417
I told her that the next day,

591
00:38:22,417 --> 00:38:24,901
I was planning to go to my parents' house.

592
00:38:26,237 --> 00:38:27,301
And?

593
00:38:27,301 --> 00:38:31,225
So the next day, she went to Nagano with me.

594
00:38:31,861 --> 00:38:33,797
That's not a reason at all.

595
00:38:33,797 --> 00:38:35,877
Yeah, that's right.

596
00:38:37,401 --> 00:38:39,241
I'm sorry.

597
00:38:39,241 --> 00:38:42,577
- So...
- Did you ask her to go with you?

598
00:38:45,429 --> 00:38:48,773
Mitsuru, did you ask her to go along?

599
00:38:49,721 --> 00:38:52,193
Yes, that's right.

600
00:38:52,193 --> 00:38:53,933
Why?

601
00:38:55,181 --> 00:38:57,157
I felt nervous.

602
00:38:59,333 --> 00:39:01,961
Forget it, I'll just ask you directly,
without choosing words.

603
00:39:01,961 --> 00:39:04,161
All right.

604
00:39:04,161 --> 00:39:06,425
You were having an affair, weren't you?

605
00:39:09,997 --> 00:39:12,533
That's right, isn't it? I'm sorry.

606
00:39:13,165 --> 00:39:16,281
Does saying "I'm sorry" mean you admit it?

607
00:39:16,281 --> 00:39:19,705
No, I'm saying there was a possibility
that you might think that,

608
00:39:19,705 --> 00:39:21,861
and I was somewhat aware of that.

609
00:39:21,861 --> 00:39:23,089
So it's not true?

610
00:39:23,089 --> 00:39:25,069
There was no affair.

611
00:39:25,785 --> 00:39:28,493
- Then what...
- It's as I said.

612
00:39:28,493 --> 00:39:31,449
Every month, we met and talked
at the laundromat. That's it.

613
00:39:31,449 --> 00:39:35,113
The day of the accident was the first time
we met outside the laundromat.

614
00:39:36,408 --> 00:39:38,933
So you expect me to just believe

615
00:39:38,933 --> 00:39:40,961
that it wasn't an affair?

616
00:39:40,961 --> 00:39:44,245
Even if that's what you say,
I'm just telling you the facts.

617
00:39:45,869 --> 00:39:48,577
Do you have any way to prove that?

618
00:39:48,577 --> 00:39:51,193
Right, where's the proof?

619
00:39:51,833 --> 00:39:54,993
I'm sure there are plenty of ways to prove
that two people are having an affair,

620
00:39:54,993 --> 00:39:58,145
but proof that there wasn't
any affair is a bit...

621
00:39:58,145 --> 00:40:00,345
So because my wife is dead,

622
00:40:01,937 --> 00:40:03,997
you think you can just say whatever you want

623
00:40:03,997 --> 00:40:06,625
and get away with it?

624
00:40:07,585 --> 00:40:09,277
That's a bit of a stretch.

625
00:40:09,277 --> 00:40:12,493
A grown man and woman, keeping
their meetings secret from their partners,

626
00:40:12,493 --> 00:40:15,905
meeting on a set day
every month at a set place,

627
00:40:15,905 --> 00:40:17,721
and in the end,

628
00:40:17,721 --> 00:40:21,057
you took her with you for an event
like visiting your estranged parents.

629
00:40:21,057 --> 00:40:23,321
And you're saying there was
nothing deep between you?

630
00:40:24,289 --> 00:40:26,993
- Hey!
- So you think she was the kind of person

631
00:40:26,993 --> 00:40:28,765
who would have an affair?

632
00:40:28,765 --> 00:40:29,877
Mitsuru, wait.

633
00:40:29,877 --> 00:40:32,869
You don't trust her, do you?
I feel sorry for you.

634
00:40:32,869 --> 00:40:34,873
- Excuse me?
- Just because a man and a woman are together,

635
00:40:34,873 --> 00:40:37,357
you jump to the conclusion that it's romance?

636
00:40:37,357 --> 00:40:38,809
That's prejudice. Must be tough.

637
00:40:38,809 --> 00:40:41,553
Were you forcing that on Mrs. Sonoda too?

638
00:40:41,553 --> 00:40:44,817
And you, a pitiful person who lost his wife,

639
00:40:44,817 --> 00:40:46,689
you think you can just ignore the facts,
flaunt your prejudice,

640
00:40:46,689 --> 00:40:48,781
and force your values on others?

641
00:41:00,521 --> 00:41:03,341
I'm sorry, I slapped him first. Again.

642
00:41:05,709 --> 00:41:08,493
I understand what you want to say,

643
00:41:08,493 --> 00:41:10,557
but as for why Azusa isn't here right now,

644
00:41:10,557 --> 00:41:12,901
you know whose fault that is, right?

645
00:41:12,901 --> 00:41:16,529
This person is Azusa's husband.

646
00:41:16,529 --> 00:41:18,417
Don't forget that.

647
00:41:19,377 --> 00:41:21,461
You need to choose your words more carefully.

648
00:41:24,953 --> 00:41:26,757
I'm sorry.

649
00:41:28,201 --> 00:41:29,941
I'm sorry.

650
00:41:40,589 --> 00:41:42,809
I was just feeling uneasy

651
00:41:42,809 --> 00:41:45,397
about visiting my parents
for the first time in a while,

652
00:41:45,397 --> 00:41:47,193
so I asked her to come along. That's all.

653
00:41:47,193 --> 00:41:50,981
But at the service area on the way
where we stopped,

654
00:41:50,981 --> 00:41:53,765
I thought that if I was going to run away,
that was the moment.

655
00:41:54,749 --> 00:41:55,953
Run away?

656
00:41:55,953 --> 00:41:58,801
I'll explain to you properly later,
about running away.

657
00:41:58,801 --> 00:42:01,773
You probably won't understand,
but I'll explain.

658
00:42:03,981 --> 00:42:07,421
I'm sorry I was the only one who survived.

659
00:42:14,669 --> 00:42:17,845
Can I ask you something too?

660
00:42:21,237 --> 00:42:25,413
What exactly is your relationship?

661
00:42:28,609 --> 00:42:31,157
Well, it's not like we have a relationship,

662
00:42:31,157 --> 00:42:33,293
I mean, it's nothing.

663
00:42:33,293 --> 00:42:35,545
She's helped me out with my son Sho,

664
00:42:35,545 --> 00:42:37,065
and I've gotten a lot of support from her.

665
00:42:37,065 --> 00:42:38,705
That goes both ways.

666
00:42:38,705 --> 00:42:42,257
There are a lot of things
I can't do alone, so he helps me out.

667
00:42:42,257 --> 00:42:44,029
No, no, I haven't really done anything.

668
00:42:45,157 --> 00:42:49,585
You know, because
our situations were similar,

669
00:42:49,585 --> 00:42:53,585
there were many things we both understood,
and we'd talk about them.

670
00:42:54,321 --> 00:42:55,593
Yes, that's all.

671
00:42:55,593 --> 00:42:59,129
Isn't that what you'd call a relationship?

672
00:42:59,129 --> 00:43:01,881
- No, it's not.
- Why would that make us have an affair?

673
00:43:01,881 --> 00:43:03,657
Where's the proof of that?

674
00:43:05,321 --> 00:43:07,113
How can you prove

675
00:43:07,113 --> 00:43:09,301
that there was no romantic involvement?

676
00:43:10,529 --> 00:43:12,821
You went into her house, didn't you?

677
00:43:12,821 --> 00:43:16,453
You helped her dispose of
my personal belongings, didn't you?

678
00:43:16,453 --> 00:43:19,865
You met with her last night, didn't you?

679
00:43:19,865 --> 00:43:23,109
Have you never been alone together
in a private room?

680
00:43:23,109 --> 00:43:26,777
Can you prove you were always
with someone else?

681
00:43:26,777 --> 00:43:30,589
How do you prove that nothing happened?

682
00:43:31,881 --> 00:43:35,841
That's exactly the same as
what you're charging me with now.

683
00:43:37,285 --> 00:43:41,397
How can you two be so sure
that it's not an affair?

684
00:43:42,361 --> 00:43:46,381
You were so suspicious of me and Mrs. Sonoda.
